# Raw input: Ultra high resolution, 8K monochrome photograph capturing Ansel Adams' iconic style of the Grand Teton mountain range in Wyoming. Snow-capped peaks dominate the frame, their jagged, wind-sculpted ridges sharply defined against a moody dawn sky. Deep shadows carve into the volcanic rock formations, while crisp, bright highlights accentuate the texture of glacial ice and pristine snowfields. A narrow valley below features a frozen river reflecting the mountain's silhouette, with frost-laden evergreen trees clinging to steep slopes. Dramatic high-contrast lighting creates ethereal mist in the foreground, enhancing the scene's timeless serenity and raw wilderness. Every grain of snow, crack in the granite, and subtle tonal gradient is rendered with photorealistic precision—rich blacks, luminous whites, and nuanced mid-tones capturing Adams' masterful control of light. Composition emphasizes grandeur through layered depth, framing the Teton's peak as the focal point with a near-perfect rule of thirds. This image embodies Adams' signature print-like quality: meticulously balanced, emotionally resonant, and technically flawless.
